#-> LAMMPS Potential File in Tersoff format.                              <-#
# Source:  N. Juslin, et al., J. Appl. Phys. 98: 123520 (2005).
#
# All entries are in "metal" units:
#   A,B [=] eV; lambda1,lambda2,lambda3 [=] 1/Angstrom; R,D [=] Angstrom
#   other quantities are unitless
#
# This particular paper makes the following symbol substitutions:
#   A = D0/(S-1)*exp(-beta_*r0*sqrt(2*S))
#   B = S*D0/(S-1)*exp(-beta_*r0*sqrt(2/S))
#   n = 1
#   m = 1
#   lambda1 = beta_*sqrt(2*S)
#   lambda2 = beta_*sqrt(2/S)
#   lambda3 = alpha_{ijk}
#   beta = omega_{ijk}
#   costheta0 = -h
#
# Entries are of the form
#   Element1 Element2 Element3 m gamma lambda3 c d costheta0 n beta lambda2
#   B R D lambda1 A
# and can be split over multiple lines as needed

